# Sustainable Fashion Research Plan Revision<br>
<br>
## Abstract<br>
<br>
This revised research plan builds upon previous work in sustainable fashion, focusing on Parisian fashion concepts that incorporate eco-friendly materials and production methods. Our goal is to create a comprehensive guide for designers and manufacturers looking to transition towards more environmentally responsible practices.<br>
<br>
## Materials Sourcing<br>
<br>
* We will prioritize sourcing materials from local suppliers whenever possible.<br>
* Consider using recycled or upcycled materials in designs.<br>
* Research sustainable fabric options, such as organic cotton, hemp, and Tencel.<br>
<br>
## Production Methods<br>
<br>
* Implement a take-back program for old garments to encourage recycling and reduce waste.<br>
* Explore the use of 3D printing technology for creating complex designs while minimizing material usage.<br>
* Investigate the potential for repurposing or upcycling existing materials in production processes.<br>
<br>
## Supply Chain Management<br>
<br>
* Develop partnerships with suppliers who share our commitment to sustainability.<br>
* Implement a system for tracking and monitoring carbon emissions throughout the supply chain.<br>
* Research the feasibility of using renewable energy sources in manufacturing facilities.<br>
<br>
```<br>
